{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Object Scaling.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Object Scaling.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"object scaling object scaling","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Object Scaling.md","fileName":"Object Scaling.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Object Scaling","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Spatial Interaction]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Interaction","Feedback","3D Manipulation","3D Travel","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Object Scaling.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Object Scaling.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"object scaling object scaling","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Object Scaling.md","fileName":"Object Scaling.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Object Scaling","heading":"Object Scaling","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Object scaling changes the size of an object. Unlike selection, positioning, and rotation, it has no direct everyday counterpart, but it is a common manipulation in two- and three-dimensional interfaces.\n\nScaling tasks vary by initial size, target size, amount of change, distance to the object, and required precision. A technique should make the scale factor and reference point clear through its mapping and [[Feedback]].\n\nObject scaling is a canonical [[3D Manipulation]] task and should remain distinct from scaling an entire world for [[3D Travel]] or viewpoint control.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Interaction","Feedback","3D Manipulation","3D Travel","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Object Scaling.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Object Scaling.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","source